where in the document?<br>\n<strong>Sebastian</strong>: Yeah, they can. I'm having trouble with the extension and comment parts.<br/>\n<strong>Mike</strong>: No problem. About the extension, remember that all the PHP files use \u201c.php\u201d as an extension; the scripts begin with \u201c< ?php\u201d and can end with \u201c? > :\u201d . In addition, keep in mind that a PHP file can contain HTML tags.", "image": "enpe7n6le02ob02re2img01.jpg", "id": 0}, {"time": "47500", "text": "<strong>Sebastian</strong>:  What about the comments?<br>\n<strong>Mike</strong>: Don't get tangled with comments. These are simply lines of text that you put in the script, but these are never read by the program. So, if you run the program, it will never be seen.<br/>\n<strong>Sebastian</strong>: How can a line be written but not read? What is its purpose then?<br/>\n<strong>Mike</strong>: As the name says, it's just a comment. Programmers put it to remind themselves of anything they did so that other developers can see their ideas, comments, or even suggestions about the script. <br/>\n<strong>Sebastian</strong>: So, a comment in PHP is just a text that appears for developers.", "image": "enpe7n6le02ob02re2img02.jpg", "id": 1}, {"time": "88000", "text": "<strong>Mike</strong>: Precisely. However, if you are having trouble with that,  there will be a problem with the case sensitivity, too.<br/>\n<strong>Sebastian</strong>: Well, I know that the keywords like if, while, and echo are not case-sensitive in PHP, but WHILE or WhiLE are the same for PHP.<br/>\n<strong>Mike</strong>: Oh! You could figure that out.<br/>\n<strong>Sebastian</strong>: Hey, I'm not dumb! Just confirm me this: keywords are not case-sensitive, but how come variables cannot be written like keywords?<br/>\n<strong>Mike</strong>: For PHP, $Color, $COLOR, and $CoLor are completely different statements because they store different information.<br/>\n<strong>Sebastian</strong>: I thought you would need more help.<br/>\n<strong>Mike</strong>: I thought it too, but if I need further information, I will let you know.", "image": "enpe7n6le02ob02re2img03.jpg", "id": 2}], "audiosrc": "enpe7n6le02ob02re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}]}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar"}]}